  "market_context": "Price was in a downtrend and tapped into a major demand zone (1.08880–1.08920), forming a W-shaped double bottom pattern, signaling potential reversal. Analyst identified this as a turning point for the current downtrend.",
  "key_observation": "A double bottom formed at the extreme demand zone (1.08880–1.08920), confirming a potential bullish reversal after price rejected the level twice.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: Identified a major level of structure (extreme demand zone) at 1.08880–1.08920 where price had previously reversed.",
    "Step 2: Observed a W-shaped double bottom pattern forming at that demand zone, indicating loss of bearish momentum and potential reversal.",
    "Step 3: Entered a long position upon confirmation of the double bottom, placing stop-loss below the swing low of the pattern.",
    "Step 4: Set target at the next higher time frame key level (HT Key Level) above current price.",
    "Step 5: Tracked profits by repositioning stop-loss below each new swing low as price broke structure upward (BOS)."
  ],
  "outcome": null,
  "lessons": "Trailing stops based on broken structure (new swing lows) allow locking in gains while letting winning trades run toward HTF key levels, maximizing risk-to-reward without premature exits.",
